WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:07.907 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: It's the season
 finale of Live Free or Die.</i>

00:00:08.007 --> 00:00:10.810 line:0%
<i> Five people
 living in the wild...</i>

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.545 line:0%
TONY: Boom shaka-laka!

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.146 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Have
 shown us their lives.</i>

00:00:14.246 --> 00:00:15.949 line:0%
COLBERT: Ever since I
was a little kid I've been

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:17.484 line:0%
dreaming about
living in the woods.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:18.751 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR:
 They've been tested.</i>

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:20.886 line:0%
THORN: It's been
two degrees at night.

00:00:20.986 --> 00:00:22.722 line:0%
GABRIEL: In California
we're in a severe drought.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.624 line:0%
Everything seems to
be dead out here.

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:26.425 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: But their
 will hasn't faltered.</i>

00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:27.660 line:0%
AMELIA: Swarm!

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.397 line:0%
TONY: Ah... I'm getting stung.

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:33.332 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: They've proven...</i>

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:35.167 line:0%
THORN: There's
no failure here.

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:37.003 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Just
 how far they can go.</i>

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:39.038 line:0%
GABRIEL: It's a big
deal to take a life.

00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:41.574 line:0%
Uh...there's the arrow.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.576 line:0%
COLBERT: I actually
built this house...every

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:45.879 line:0%
screw...every nail
and now it's gone.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:47.880 line:0%
<i> [Thorn screams].</i>

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:50.449 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Now
 they're fight continues.</i>

00:00:50.549 --> 00:00:52.017 line:0%
GABRIEL: I don't
have too many choices;

00:00:52.117 --> 00:00:54.720 line:0%
I've got to
catch a couple fish.

00:00:54.987 --> 00:00:57.122 line:0%
THORN: My little girl
Briar is just so sick.

00:00:57.222 --> 00:00:58.357 line:0%
<i> [Briar coughing].</i>

00:00:58.457 --> 00:01:00.226 line:0%
I've got to get
some medicine.

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.662 line:0%
COLBERT: I'm rebuilding
my home with my family.

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:06.332 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Because their
 quest to live free never ends.</i>

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:09.035 line:0%
TONY: This is the way
that we want to live.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:11.670 line:0%
It'll be that way
until the day I die.

00:01:12.571 --> 00:01:15.674 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: There is a
 movement growing in America.</i>

00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:19.278 line:0%
<i> These pioneers
 have made a choice...</i>

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:24.884 line:0%
<i> To awaken the animal self
 by going back to the wild.</i>

00:01:40.966 --> 00:01:44.336 line:0%
GABRIEL: It's
windier than I thought.

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:48.208 line:0%
Alright...I'm
gonna try my luck.

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:51.611 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: In
 California...nomadic hunter</i>

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:53.879 line:0%
<i> Gabriel is about to
 begin the final leg of his</i>

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:55.815 line:0%
<i> grueling journey.</i>

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:58.384 line:0%
<i> Having trekked nearly 40
 miles from the mountain</i>

00:01:58.484 --> 00:02:01.721 line:0%
<i> cabin where he spent the
 past several months...</i>

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:03.656 line:0%
<i> Gabriel is now
 headed down the coast...</i>

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:06.426 line:0%
<i> home to his fiancé Luna.</i>

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:08.294 line:0%
GABRIEL: This has been
an awesome experience out

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:09.696 line:0%
on the land.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.697 line:0%
But at the same time
I'm engaged to Luna.

00:02:11.797 --> 00:02:13.466 line:0%
We've been
together ten years.

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:16.668 line:0%
It's time for us to start
the next chapter together.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.704 line:0%
A lot of the times we
go out on journeys...

00:02:18.804 --> 00:02:20.540 line:0%
I'm hunting or fishing or
gathering some kind of food

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.377 line:0%
source to bring home for
Luna and for both of us and

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:28.414 line:0%
so I usually don't like
to come home empty-handed.

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:31.317 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Gabriel will
 try his luck using a simple</i>

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:33.118 line:0%
<i> improvised hand line.</i>

00:02:33.218 --> 00:02:36.089 line:0%
GABRIEL: I've got my yucca
with a good hook on the end.

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:38.824 line:0%
I'm gonna go get some
mussels out before the tide

00:02:38.924 --> 00:02:40.793 line:0%
comes in too much.

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:42.895 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: But heavy
 ocean currents will make it</i>

00:02:42.995 --> 00:02:45.898 line:0%
<i> challenging to
 keep the line steady.</i>

00:02:45.998 --> 00:02:47.900 line:0%
GABRIEL: It's crazy
out here right now.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.269 line:0%
It's like full storm surge.

00:02:50.369 --> 00:02:52.105 line:0%
It's a hard time to
be out in the water.

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:54.307 line:0%
It's kind of dangerous
'cause there's rip tides and

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:57.509 line:0%
waves moving everywhere.

00:02:57.776 --> 00:03:01.246 line:0%
Alright that should be good.

00:03:01.346 --> 00:03:04.416 line:0%
Let's get out there.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:08.888 line:0%
So basically I'm gonna head
out here and tie myself into

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:12.058 line:0%
the kelp and try to drop my
hand line down into the kelp

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:14.861 line:0%
bed all the way
to the bottom.

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:17.730 line:0%
I have to be careful of
the waves...the current...

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:20.767 line:0%
the wind and
also the sharks.

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:24.604 line:0%
The ocean kills
people really easy.

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:27.773 line:0%
It's a place where if you
don't know how to move and

00:03:27.873 --> 00:03:32.045 line:0%
bend with the currents
then it'll take you under.

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:42.821 line:0%
It's not the best time to be
fishing in the kelp bed but

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.891 line:0%
I don't have
too many choices.

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:47.693 line:0%
I gotta catch a couple fish.

00:03:47.926 --> 00:03:50.363 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: With escalating
 gale force winds and choppy</i>

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:55.735 line:0%
<i> heaving swells Gabriel's
 quest for a fish is risky.</i>

00:03:57.736 --> 00:04:01.040 line:0%
GABRIEL: It's pretty
crazy lumpy right now.

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:04.711 line:0%
There's a big riptide.

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:07.146 line:0%
Ohhh!

00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:13.719 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: While Gabriel
 struggles against the</i>

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:16.555 line:0%
<i> ocean's currents...
 in North Carolina...</i>

00:04:16.655 --> 00:04:18.757 line:0%
<i> homesteaders Tony and
 Amelia are testing out a</i>

00:04:18.857 --> 00:04:21.561 line:0%
<i> new way to feed
 their chickens.</i>

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:23.363 line:0%
AMELIA: They're
gonna love this...

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:25.130 line:0%
c'mon chickens.

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:26.732 line:0%
TONY: C'mon boogies.

00:04:26.832 --> 00:04:30.069 line:0%
AMELIA: Woooo...oh my God!

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:32.972 line:0%
We've got thousands
and thousands of maggots

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:34.406 line:0%
in this bucket.

00:04:34.506 --> 00:04:37.477 line:0%
They're eating what
was once a ground hog...

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:41.180 line:0%
has basically
turned into nothing.

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:44.650 line:0%
Flies have flown in
through the top holes...

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:48.988 line:0%
they've laid eggs on the
roadkill and the eggs...

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:51.190 line:0%
which are turning
into maggots...

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:53.159 line:0%
are falling out
of the bottom.

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:55.661 line:0%
TONY: It's raining maggots.

00:04:55.761 --> 00:04:58.630 line:0%
AMELIA: Alright
chickens...go for it.

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:00.499 line:0%
TONY: There they go.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:03.102 line:0%
AMELIA: These maggots
are extremely nutritious

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:04.169 line:0%
for the chickens.

00:05:04.269 --> 00:05:06.005 line:0%
They give them
plenty of protein.

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:09.275 line:0%
TONY: Maggot showers
equals happy chickens.

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:13.913 line:0%
Happy chickens
equals delicious eggs.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:20.052 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Tony and Amelia
 have dedicated their lives</i>

00:05:20.152 --> 00:05:22.455 line:0%
<i> to being entirely
 self-sufficient.</i>

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:25.057 line:0%
<i> But finding a way to
 eat only what they grow</i>

00:05:25.157 --> 00:05:26.792 line:0%
<i> has been a challenge.</i>

00:05:26.892 --> 00:05:28.594 line:0%
TONY: Three years
we've been here.

00:05:28.694 --> 00:05:29.828 line:0%
AMELIA: Yeah.

00:05:29.928 --> 00:05:32.564 line:0%
TONY: We've done pretty
good for three years of swale

00:05:32.664 --> 00:05:34.900 line:0%
digging and tree planting.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:37.836 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Tony and Amelia
 fought every possible element</i>

00:05:37.936 --> 00:05:40.506 line:0%
<i> to turn this
 uninhabitable hill into a</i>

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:43.108 line:0%
<i> fully sustainable homestead.</i>

00:05:43.208 --> 00:05:44.676 line:0%
TONY: So you know
what we should do today?

00:05:44.776 --> 00:05:45.777 line:0%
AMELIA: What's that?

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:47.413 line:0%
TONY: We should have a
little feasting on the

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:50.816 line:0%
forest garden to celebrate our
three-year land anniversary.

00:05:50.916 --> 00:05:53.085 line:0%
We've got plenty of
vegetables to eat.

00:05:53.185 --> 00:05:54.120 line:0%
AMELIA: Yeah.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:56.589 line:0%
TONY: Let's do it.

00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:58.458 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Before
 the harvest begins...</i>

00:05:58.558 --> 00:06:01.060 line:0%
<i> Tony's gonna make use of
something else from the garden.</i>

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.195 line:0%
TONY: So it's Amelia and I's
three-year anniversary of

00:06:03.295 --> 00:06:06.365 line:0%
living on the land together
and I'm wanting to make

00:06:06.465 --> 00:06:10.403 line:0%
Amelia something really cool
for an anniversary present.

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:15.408 line:0%
We're dealing with
some foul (bleep) here.

00:06:16.342 --> 00:06:19.112 line:0%
This pig came from our
neighbor's pig that we

00:06:19.212 --> 00:06:22.982 line:0%
helped slaughter.

00:06:26.818 --> 00:06:29.622 line:0%
It's pretty "F'ing" gross.

00:06:31.089 --> 00:06:32.591 line:0%
I saw the teeth
and I was like...

00:06:32.691 --> 00:06:34.360 line:0%
"God those teeth
are really cool."

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.728 line:0%
So I could make a really
cool you know cavewoman

00:06:36.828 --> 00:06:39.332 line:0%
necklace for Amelia.

00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:41.934 line:0%
I think Amelia will be
stoked that I had the nerve

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:44.736 line:0%
to pull these teeth out
and touch this greasy...

00:06:44.836 --> 00:06:50.042 line:0%
stinky pig remnants.

00:06:50.142 --> 00:06:52.978 line:0%
I'm a little nervous
that I'm going to vomit.

00:06:53.445 --> 00:06:55.748 line:0%
Yeah...hell no.

00:06:55.848 --> 00:06:57.049 line:0%
AMELIA: Are you gonna vomit?

00:06:57.149 --> 00:06:59.085 line:0%
TONY: I'm alright.

00:06:59.185 --> 00:07:03.523 line:0%
Yeah...ugh...ugh!

00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:09.361 line:0%
Actually I'm just
not gonna do this.

00:07:09.461 --> 00:07:10.796 line:0%
No I have to.

00:07:10.896 --> 00:07:12.564 line:0%
I gotta get 'er done.

00:07:12.665 --> 00:07:14.466 line:0%
I'm gonna have to
muster up the will to touch

00:07:14.566 --> 00:07:16.402 line:0%
a rotten pig's head
to get the teeth out.

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:20.406 line:0%
These are the things that
a person will do for love.

00:07:20.506 --> 00:07:22.775 line:0%
These aren't really budging.

00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:26.111 line:0%
I think we can come
back to these later.

00:07:26.211 --> 00:07:29.348 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: As Tony mulls
 over pulling pig's teeth...</i>

00:07:29.448 --> 00:07:31.851 line:0%
<i> five and a half
 miles over the ridge...</i>

00:07:31.951 --> 00:07:34.219 line:0%
<i> primitive woodsman
 Thorn is beginning a project</i>

00:07:34.319 --> 00:07:35.554 line:0%
<i> of his own.</i>

00:07:35.655 --> 00:07:37.390 line:0%
THORN: My new shelter's
looking really good.

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:38.958 line:0%
I'm pretty proud.

00:07:39.058 --> 00:07:42.128 line:0%
It's awesome to have the
difficult things out of the

00:07:42.228 --> 00:07:45.230 line:0%
way and now I can move
onto a little bit more of

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:46.398 line:0%
the fun stuff.

00:07:46.498 --> 00:07:48.301 line:0%
You know what I was
thinking about doing today?

00:07:48.401 --> 00:07:50.736 line:0%
I wanna build a
bunk bed with you.

00:07:50.836 --> 00:07:52.637 line:0%
I have my bed finished.

00:07:52.738 --> 00:07:54.406 line:0%
BRIAR: I thought
that was my bed!

00:07:54.506 --> 00:07:58.611 line:0%
No...I'm gonna build
you one a little higher up.

00:07:59.945 --> 00:08:02.181 line:0%
BRIAR: Don't forget you
should have shoes on.

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:03.416 line:0%
THORN: I'm good.

00:08:03.516 --> 00:08:04.984 line:0%
BRIAR: Ok you're good.

00:08:05.084 --> 00:08:08.520 line:0%
THORN: Out here I've got
a really enormous forest to

00:08:08.621 --> 00:08:13.158 line:0%
pull resources out of
and I'm really lucky.

00:08:14.025 --> 00:08:16.395 line:0%
It's not like
buying all the lumber.

00:08:16.495 --> 00:08:18.397 line:0%
This is my lumber yard.

00:08:18.497 --> 00:08:20.266 line:0%
BRIAR: Daddy...I'm
getting so excited.

00:08:20.366 --> 00:08:22.367 line:0%
THORN: I know... I'm
excited too for you.

00:08:22.468 --> 00:08:24.670 line:0%
I might be more thrilled
than she is because it's

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:26.538 line:0%
really hard to
sleep with her.

00:08:26.638 --> 00:08:28.841 line:0%
She just kicks me
all night long.

00:08:28.941 --> 00:08:30.576 line:0%
I don't know what she's
dreaming about but it's

00:08:30.676 --> 00:08:32.211 line:0%
gotta have something to
do with fighting a bunch

00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:35.281 line:0%
of Ninjas off.

00:08:37.716 --> 00:08:39.919 line:0%
Back where we moved
from in our house...

00:08:40.019 --> 00:08:41.253 line:0%
we had a bunk bed.

00:08:41.353 --> 00:08:42.921 line:0%
And I built it for
her it was awesome.

00:08:43.021 --> 00:08:44.356 line:0%
I knew she loved it.

00:08:44.456 --> 00:08:46.291 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: The A-frame
 structure of Thorn's new</i>

00:08:46.391 --> 00:08:48.694 line:0%
<i> shelter will allow him
 to frame two crossbeams</i>

00:08:48.794 --> 00:08:52.231 line:0%
<i> directly above
 his existing bed.</i>

00:08:55.167 --> 00:08:58.404 line:0%
BRIAR: Daddy... you're
making a mess in here!

00:08:58.504 --> 00:09:00.305 line:0%
THORN: Yeah.

00:09:00.405 --> 00:09:03.976 line:0%
<i> [hammering].</i>

00:09:06.678 --> 00:09:09.181 line:0%
BRIAR: Yeah it's
almost there I think.

00:09:09.281 --> 00:09:11.483 line:0%
THORN: Just
gotta make a ladder.

00:09:11.583 --> 00:09:16.556 line:0%
I'm really appreciating
having this open floor plan.

00:09:17.889 --> 00:09:21.794 line:0%
At some point in the future
I can move onto some walls

00:09:21.894 --> 00:09:25.364 line:0%
but I don't need to do
that until the fall.

00:09:26.164 --> 00:09:29.268 line:0%
That's pretty good.

00:09:32.337 --> 00:09:34.373 line:0%
Check it out.

00:09:34.473 --> 00:09:36.641 line:0%
BRIAR: I can even
stand up a little.

00:09:36.742 --> 00:09:38.844 line:0%
THORN: Yeah...
just a little?

00:09:38.944 --> 00:09:41.747 line:0%
Briar's totally into it...
she loves it.

00:09:41.847 --> 00:09:44.817 line:0%
It's not a huge bunk bed
but it's not a huge house.

00:09:44.917 --> 00:09:47.252 line:0%
I think I'm gonna
sleep better tonight too.

00:09:47.352 --> 00:09:49.755 line:0%
It's win-win.

00:09:49.855 --> 00:09:52.191 line:0%
<i> [Briar coughing].</i>

00:09:52.291 --> 00:09:54.126 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: But any plans
 for today will have to be</i>

00:09:54.226 --> 00:09:56.862 line:0%
<i> put on hold as Briar's
 nagging cough has taken a</i>

00:09:56.962 --> 00:09:58.730 line:0%
<i> turn for the worse.</i>

00:09:58.830 --> 00:10:00.432 line:0%
<i> [Briar coughing].</i>

00:10:00.532 --> 00:10:02.334 line:0%
THORN: It's not a good one.

00:10:02.434 --> 00:10:05.371 line:0%
My little girl Briar...
she's pretty sick right now.

00:10:05.571 --> 00:10:07.506 line:0%
<i> [Briar coughing].</i>

00:10:07.606 --> 00:10:09.441 line:0%
You want some medicine?

00:10:09.541 --> 00:10:11.910 line:0%
I'm just about out.

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:16.048 line:0%
I'm running low on
medicine and I really need to

00:10:16.148 --> 00:10:18.350 line:0%
attend to this cough.

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:21.153 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: As Thorn cares
 for his sick daughter...</i>

00:10:21.253 --> 00:10:23.822 line:0%
<i> in the swamp of south
 Georgia frontiersman</i>

00:10:23.922 --> 00:10:27.293 line:0%
<i> Colbert's grandchildren have
 come to help him rebuild.</i>

00:10:28.927 --> 00:10:30.329 line:0%
COLBERT: You
remember the cabin?

00:10:30.429 --> 00:10:33.398 line:0%
They've been coming since
they were little bitty kids

00:10:33.498 --> 00:10:35.534 line:0%
and it's great to have all
four of them come at one

00:10:35.634 --> 00:10:37.302 line:0%
time to share in the fun.

00:10:37.402 --> 00:10:39.938 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: This is their
 first visit since his cabin</i>

00:10:40.038 --> 00:10:42.207 line:0%
<i> burned down this winter.</i>

00:10:42.307 --> 00:10:43.809 line:0%
COLBERT: Now this
is a super antique.

00:10:43.909 --> 00:10:45.977 line:0%
This is over 100 year-old
screwdriver and it had a

00:10:46.077 --> 00:10:47.746 line:0%
wooden handle on it.

00:10:47.846 --> 00:10:49.948 line:0%
CODY: So many
memories in that place and

00:10:50.048 --> 00:10:52.585 line:0%
now it's just gone.

00:10:52.685 --> 00:10:54.219 line:0%
COLBERT: Do you
recognize what this is?

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.522 line:0%
DEVON: That
would be the .22.

00:10:56.622 --> 00:11:00.593 line:0%
We always used to sit out on
the porch and just basically

00:11:00.693 --> 00:11:03.262 line:0%
tell jokes all night.

00:11:03.362 --> 00:11:05.264 line:0%
COLBERT: Everything
in life is temporary and

00:11:05.364 --> 00:11:07.266 line:0%
everything is precious.

00:11:07.366 --> 00:11:09.334 line:0%
It's always a traumatic
experience when you lose

00:11:09.434 --> 00:11:11.704 line:0%
something that we
put a lot of value on.

00:11:11.804 --> 00:11:15.040 line:0%
To me...to help me make a
transition of letting go of

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:19.478 line:0%
emotional attachment to
material things I guess

00:11:19.578 --> 00:11:23.582 line:0%
that's a lesson I
needed to learn.

00:11:24.282 --> 00:11:26.819 line:0%
So I've been dragging
all this new logs in to

00:11:26.919 --> 00:11:28.587 line:0%
rebuild the cabin.

00:11:28.687 --> 00:11:30.923 line:0%
So we're gonna dig a
hole to put the pole in.

00:11:31.023 --> 00:11:33.125 line:0%
I remember putting up
the very first pole.

00:11:33.225 --> 00:11:36.161 line:0%
That's been 24 years ago.

00:11:36.261 --> 00:11:39.064 line:0%
That first erection to start
the process to figure out

00:11:39.164 --> 00:11:42.201 line:0%
where to put the
deck and the frame.

00:11:42.301 --> 00:11:45.071 line:0%
We're gonna stand the first
pole up here so we can build

00:11:45.171 --> 00:11:47.807 line:0%
a cabin on posts.

00:11:47.907 --> 00:11:50.909 line:0%
You think that hole's big
enough for that post to fit in?

00:11:51.009 --> 00:11:52.277 line:0%
CODY: It'll slip right in.

00:11:52.378 --> 00:11:54.780 line:0%
COLBERT: Cody go measure
the pole like this and

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:57.349 line:0%
see if it's
this wide or wider.

00:11:57.450 --> 00:12:00.185 line:0%
See if it's big enough
to fit down in the hole.

00:12:00.285 --> 00:12:02.955 line:0%
What about the other way?

00:12:03.055 --> 00:12:04.189 line:0%
CODY: Nope.

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:05.991 line:0%
COLBERT: So what we have
to do is we have to make

00:12:06.091 --> 00:12:09.728 line:0%
the hole a little bit wider.

00:12:09.828 --> 00:12:12.498 line:0%
How do you like our rulers?

00:12:12.598 --> 00:12:14.567 line:0%
To me this is a
really big deal.

00:12:14.667 --> 00:12:17.102 line:0%
I'm rebuilding my home a
home I'm going to share with

00:12:17.202 --> 00:12:20.840 line:0%
my family with my grandkids
so as they get older they'll

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:23.776 line:0%
not only have Grandpa's
cabin to go to but they'll

00:12:23.876 --> 00:12:27.947 line:0%
remember how they
helped put it together.

00:12:29.681 --> 00:12:31.884 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Colbert's fire
 damaged tools throw a wrench</i>

00:12:31.984 --> 00:12:37.523 line:0%
<i> in his plans and Tony goes
 to great lengths for love.</i>

00:12:38.324 --> 00:12:40.392 line:0%
TONY: There's still like
some smushy bits on this thing.

00:12:40.492 --> 00:12:42.161 line:0%
<i> [gagging]</i>

00:12:51.837 --> 00:12:54.440 line:0%
GABRIEL: It's not the best
time to be fishing in the

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:58.210 line:0%
kelp bed but I gotta
catch a couple fish.

00:12:58.310 --> 00:13:00.679 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Off the coast
 of California Gabriel is</i>

00:13:00.779 --> 00:13:03.716 line:0%
<i> battling the unforgiving
 ocean currents in hopes of</i>

00:13:03.816 --> 00:13:06.618 line:0%
<i> catching a fish.</i>

00:13:06.818 --> 00:13:10.489 line:0%
GABRIEL: There's a
big riptide...Ohh!

00:13:20.999 --> 00:13:22.801 line:0%
It's crazy out here.

00:13:22.901 --> 00:13:26.037 line:0%
This is like 35-40
knot gale force winds...

00:13:26.137 --> 00:13:29.842 line:0%
which doesn't
happen very often.

00:13:29.942 --> 00:13:31.877 line:0%
I think I gotta go in.

00:13:31.977 --> 00:13:34.579 line:0%
No fish today.

00:13:34.679 --> 00:13:37.482 line:0%
It was almost impossible
just to get the hook to go

00:13:37.582 --> 00:13:41.753 line:0%
down to the bottom because
of all the current and chop.

00:13:41.853 --> 00:13:45.123 line:0%
It didn't go too well but
maybe tomorrow when it calms

00:13:45.223 --> 00:13:50.596 line:0%
down a little bit in the
morning I'll have better luck.

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:53.665 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: With no luck
 on the ocean Gabriel has</i>

00:13:53.765 --> 00:13:56.568 line:0%
<i> no choice but to
 eat his own bait.</i>

00:13:56.668 --> 00:13:59.071 line:0%
GABRIEL: I think my best bet
is to take the mussels that

00:13:59.171 --> 00:14:03.775 line:0%
I got for fishing and
cook a few of those up.

00:14:03.875 --> 00:14:07.980 line:0%
You wanna cook 'em
until they pop open.

00:14:08.447 --> 00:14:11.750 line:0%
Now these mussels are one of
my favorite things to eat.

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:15.054 line:0%
But mussels collect toxins
in the water that can make

00:14:15.154 --> 00:14:18.690 line:0%
