and also kill you.

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:23.895 line:0%
With mussels you can test it
by touching your tongue to

00:14:23.995 --> 00:14:27.566 line:0%
the mussel and if you get
like a numbness in your

00:14:27.666 --> 00:14:30.769 line:0%
mouth then you know
there's toxins in there.

00:14:30.869 --> 00:14:35.307 line:0%
There's a little tiny bit
of a kind of twinge but I'm

00:14:35.407 --> 00:14:37.376 line:0%
kind of testing my
fate 'cause I'm pretty

00:14:37.476 --> 00:14:40.279 line:0%
hungry right now.

00:14:45.083 --> 00:14:48.287 line:0%
So good...alright.

00:14:48.387 --> 00:14:50.956 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Hoping that he
 hasn't eaten toxic mussels</i>

00:14:51.056 --> 00:14:52.858 line:0%
<i> Gabriel calls it a night.</i>

00:14:52.958 --> 00:14:55.160 line:0%
GABRIEL: I'm gonna head over
to my little nest and get up

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:57.396 line:0%
with the sun early in
the morning and see if the

00:14:57.496 --> 00:15:00.865 line:0%
wind's dead so I can try
another day and see if I can

00:15:00.965 --> 00:15:04.603 line:0%
catch some fish.

00:15:21.352 --> 00:15:22.788 line:0%
TONY: We gonna get
some vegetables?

00:15:22.888 --> 00:15:24.189 line:0%
AMELIA: Yes.

00:15:24.289 --> 00:15:25.657 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Back in
 North Carolina...</i>

00:15:25.757 --> 00:15:27.526 line:0%
<i> homesteaders Tony and
 Amelia are planning a</i>

00:15:27.626 --> 00:15:29.862 line:0%
<i> celebration to mark the
three-year anniversary of their</i>

00:15:29.962 --> 00:15:32.097 line:0%
<i> life together on the land.</i>

00:15:32.197 --> 00:15:34.833 line:0%
TONY: Should we
get some sochan?

00:15:34.933 --> 00:15:36.034 line:0%
AMELIA: Why not?

00:15:36.134 --> 00:15:37.502 line:0%
TONY: Let's get some sochan.

00:15:37.602 --> 00:15:38.837 line:0%
AMELIA: I wanna
get everything.

00:15:38.937 --> 00:15:40.873 line:0%
I wanna have like
a nice big feast.

00:15:40.973 --> 00:15:42.674 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: But with the
abundance of plant life growing</i>

00:15:42.775 --> 00:15:44.709 line:0%
<i> on their hillside
 deciding what to eat is</i>

00:15:44.809 --> 00:15:47.346 line:0%
<i> going to be tough.</i>

00:15:50.849 --> 00:15:52.117 line:0%
AMELIA: Hey look!

00:15:52.217 --> 00:15:53.885 line:0%
There's a bunch of
oyster mushrooms!

00:15:53.985 --> 00:15:55.854 line:0%
TONY: Cool.

00:15:55.954 --> 00:15:58.390 line:0%
Everything here is
here for a reason.

00:15:58.490 --> 00:16:00.993 line:0%
Above and below ground
there's more going on than

00:16:01.093 --> 00:16:04.863 line:0%
you can even conceive here
than you can even understand.

00:16:04.963 --> 00:16:06.865 line:0%
AMELIA: I think this is
the biggest wild strawberry

00:16:06.965 --> 00:16:09.034 line:0%
patch we have right here.

00:16:09.134 --> 00:16:11.303 line:0%
TONY: We're creating
this web of symbiotic

00:16:11.403 --> 00:16:13.471 line:0%
relationships with plants
and animals and fungi and

00:16:13.572 --> 00:16:16.108 line:0%
water and soil and sun
that take care of us and

00:16:16.208 --> 00:16:17.842 line:0%
meet our needs.

00:16:17.942 --> 00:16:20.112 line:0%
AMELIA: The dandelion
greens came up.

00:16:20.212 --> 00:16:22.214 line:0%
TONY: It's crazy to think
about how much people spend

00:16:22.314 --> 00:16:25.350 line:0%
