in the grocery store.

00:16:25.451 --> 00:16:29.020 line:0%
Stuff like
almost grows wild.

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:31.190 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: 20% of fresh
 fruits and vegetables in</i>

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:34.760 line:0%
<i> today's modern supermarket
 spoil and get thrown away.</i>

00:16:34.860 --> 00:16:38.563 line:0%
<i> This forces grocery stores
 to charge a 75% markup or</i>

00:16:38.663 --> 00:16:42.468 line:0%
<i> more to offset the loss.</i>

00:16:45.704 --> 00:16:48.574 line:0%
TONY: I just got
a grasshopper.

00:16:50.342 --> 00:16:53.979 line:0%
They're starting to get
big this time of year.

00:16:57.082 --> 00:16:59.284 line:0%
Well I just think that
communities should just take

00:16:59.384 --> 00:17:01.019 line:0%
it upon themselves
to be resilient.

00:17:01.119 --> 00:17:03.655 line:0%
Instead some of the folks
have to drive off to the

00:17:03.755 --> 00:17:06.491 line:0%
city to like make money to
pay their mortgage to buy

00:17:06.592 --> 00:17:09.194 line:0%
pop tarts at the store
to make themselves sick.

00:17:09.294 --> 00:17:11.630 line:0%
It just it's not
making any sense.

00:17:11.730 --> 00:17:13.465 line:0%
You know let's
get some honey.

00:17:13.565 --> 00:17:16.367 line:0%
Real things like soil and
water and community that's

00:17:16.468 --> 00:17:19.971 line:0%
the way that we build in
resilience to our lives.

00:17:20.072 --> 00:17:22.107 line:0%
Not by having a stack of
cash that has nothing to

00:17:22.207 --> 00:17:24.376 line:0%
back it that you can
set on fire then you don't

00:17:24.476 --> 00:17:25.744 line:0%
have it anymore.

00:17:25.844 --> 00:17:27.111 line:0%
You know.

00:17:27.212 --> 00:17:29.348 line:0%
AMELIA: Ooh...look at
all those milk weeds.

00:17:29.448 --> 00:17:32.584 line:0%
TONY: But if you have
skills and materials then

00:17:32.684 --> 00:17:34.286 line:0%
you're good...you're safe.

00:17:34.386 --> 00:17:37.088 line:0%
You're safer than
a lot of people.

00:17:37.188 --> 00:17:40.192 line:0%
AMELIA: Let's see if there's
any wild strawberries down here.

00:17:40.292 --> 00:17:44.563 line:0%
TONY: Oh hell yeah...
I wanna have that.

00:17:54.839 --> 00:17:56.708 line:0%
COLBERT: What you do right
here when you're not getting

00:17:56.808 --> 00:17:58.844 line:0%
any dirt is you have
to poke like this and

00:17:58.944 --> 00:18:00.979 line:0%
break some dirt loose.

00:18:01.079 --> 00:18:03.582 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: In Georgia
 Colbert's grandchildren are</i>

00:18:03.682 --> 00:18:05.817 line:0%
<i> helping him
 rebuild his cabin.</i>

00:18:05.917 --> 00:18:07.486 line:0%
COLBERT: Who's having fun?

00:18:07.586 --> 00:18:09.755 line:0%
Whoopee!

00:18:09.855 --> 00:18:11.957 line:0%
We're gonna start the
process move one of the

00:18:12.057 --> 00:18:14.025 line:0%
