the technique and then we'll

00:18:14.125 --> 00:18:15.760 line:0%
start lifting the pole.

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:18.263 line:0%
It's gonna be hard to set
in the ground but we're all

00:18:18.363 --> 00:18:20.699 line:0%
gonna participate in the
process of starting the

00:18:20.799 --> 00:18:22.100 line:0%
building project.

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:24.503 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: The first step is
 to place utility poles deep</i>

00:18:24.603 --> 00:18:27.372 line:0%
<i> in the ground to
 provide a solid foundation.</i>

00:18:27.472 --> 00:18:28.940 line:0%
COLBERT: Now who wants
to pick up the post and

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:30.142 line:0%
throw it in a hole.

00:18:30.242 --> 00:18:31.610 line:0%
Can you pick it up
and throw it in there?

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:33.111 line:0%
Why not?

00:18:33.211 --> 00:18:34.513 line:0%
GRANDKID: It's too heavy.

00:18:34.613 --> 00:18:36.347 line:0%
CODY: Because he's weak.

00:18:36.447 --> 00:18:39.317 line:0%
COLBERT: Let me
show you a trick.

00:18:39.417 --> 00:18:42.787 line:0%
So what we're gonna do is
we're gonna hook this on here.

00:18:42.887 --> 00:18:45.090 line:0%
So you slip it down
here till it's tight.

00:18:45.190 --> 00:18:47.592 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Colbert uses
 a rope and pulley system</i>

00:18:47.692 --> 00:18:49.561 line:0%
<i> to create a
 mechanical advantage.</i>

00:18:49.661 --> 00:18:51.663 line:0%
COLBERT: If you push it
down like that then it slips.

00:18:51.763 --> 00:18:54.066 line:0%
But if you lift the
rope up then it locks.

00:18:54.166 --> 00:18:56.101 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: The system
 requires less force by</i>

00:18:56.201 --> 00:18:58.369 line:0%
<i> transferring the weight of
 the pole to the pulley and</i>

00:18:58.469 --> 00:19:01.239 line:0%
<i> rope making it
 easier to move.</i>

00:19:01.339 --> 00:19:04.342 line:0%
COLBERT: Now be careful
and see if you can get that

00:19:04.443 --> 00:19:07.546 line:0%
log to jump up
and go that way.

00:19:09.147 --> 00:19:10.682 line:0%
Look at that.

00:19:10.782 --> 00:19:13.852 line:0%
I think Chase is
stronger than Cody.

00:19:13.952 --> 00:19:16.722 line:0%
CODY: No.

00:19:18.156 --> 00:19:20.392 line:0%
COLBERT: As we lift this up
there's gonna be a lot of

00:19:20.492 --> 00:19:23.761 line:0%
pressure on the bottom end
the whole weight of the pole.

00:19:23.862 --> 00:19:26.498 line:0%
The problem with this is
that it went through the

00:19:26.598 --> 00:19:30.635 line:0%
fire and it's really
rusty and it might not work.

00:19:30.735 --> 00:19:32.938 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: To start building
 the new foundation for his</i>

00:19:33.038 --> 00:19:35.173 line:0%
<i> cabin Colbert and his
 grandchildren will need to</i>

00:19:35.273 --> 00:19:38.877 line:0%
<i> hoist this 400-pound utility
 pole to a 90-degree angle</i>

00:19:38.977 --> 00:19:41.012 line:0%
<i> and anchor it in place.</i>

00:19:41.112 --> 00:19:42.847 line:0%
COLBERT: If we start to
stand that up what could

00:19:42.947 --> 00:19:44.249 line:0%
possibly go wrong?

00:19:44.349 --> 00:19:46.084 line:0%
CODY: It could kill someone.

00:19:46.185 --> 00:19:48.353 line:0%
COLBERT: If that falls
where do you wanna be?

00:19:48.453 --> 00:19:49.655 line:0%
CODY: Out of the way.

00:19:49.755 --> 00:19:52.390 line:0%
COLBERT: Out of the way.

00:19:52.490 --> 00:19:55.293 line:0%
Does everybody
understand their job?

00:19:55.393 --> 00:19:57.863 line:0%
Everybody ready?

00:19:59.664 --> 00:20:02.334 line:0%
A little more Devon...

00:20:05.437 --> 00:20:08.307 line:0%
Oh (bleep).

00:20:14.012 --> 00:20:15.680 line:0%
COLBERT: Is everybody ready?

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:18.149 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: In the Georgia
 swamp frontiersman Colbert</i>

00:20:18.249 --> 00:20:20.251 line:0%
<i> and his grandchildren
 are attempting to stand a</i>

00:20:20.352 --> 00:20:22.821 line:0%
<i> 400-pound utility
 pole in the ground for</i>

00:20:22.921 --> 00:20:25.657 line:0%
<i> the cabin's foundation.</i>

00:20:27.626 --> 00:20:29.394 line:0%
DEVON: I bottomed out.

00:20:29.494 --> 00:20:30.862 line:0%
COLBERT: I see the problem.

00:20:30.962 --> 00:20:32.630 line:0%
Since he can't travel
anymore we have to figure

00:20:32.730 --> 00:20:34.799 line:0%
out something else to do.

00:20:34.899 --> 00:20:36.968 line:0%
Give yourself some slack and
move the slippery rope farther

00:20:37.068 --> 00:20:39.838 line:0%
to the end of the pole.

00:20:39.938 --> 00:20:42.507 line:0%
If we don't slip the anchor
point up higher on the pole

00:20:42.607 --> 00:20:45.176 line:0%
it'll make a great deal of
effort and stress but at the

00:20:45.276 --> 00:20:47.646 line:0%
