push it up with our hands.

00:20:47.746 --> 00:20:50.782 line:0%
I want you guys to start
pulling and help me lift it.

00:20:50.882 --> 00:20:52.216 line:0%
You guys ready?

00:20:52.316 --> 00:20:53.651 line:0%
GRANDKIDS: Yeah.

00:20:53.751 --> 00:20:55.988 line:0%
COLBERT: 1...2...3.

00:21:08.399 --> 00:21:12.136 line:0%
Ayyyy the pole's in!

00:21:12.336 --> 00:21:14.706 line:0%
We did the impossible with
simple tools and we did it

00:21:14.806 --> 00:21:15.907 line:0%
as a family.

00:21:16.007 --> 00:21:17.008 line:0%
CODY: That's pretty awesome.

00:21:17.108 --> 00:21:18.143 line:0%
COLBERT: Pretty awesome.

00:21:18.243 --> 00:21:20.045 line:0%
CODY: That's pretty awesome.

00:21:20.145 --> 00:21:21.780 line:0%
COLBERT: This may
not look like a lot.

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.114 line:0%
Just a big utility pole.

00:21:23.214 --> 00:21:25.684 line:0%
But to me it's the
beginning start of my home.

00:21:25.784 --> 00:21:27.819 line:0%
The most important step
in any long journey is the

00:21:27.919 --> 00:21:31.956 line:0%
first step and I've
got the first step done.

00:21:32.056 --> 00:21:33.191 line:0%
There you go.

00:21:33.291 --> 00:21:36.260 line:0%
That's straight up and down.

00:21:36.561 --> 00:21:38.530 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: With the
 hard work behind them it's</i>

00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:39.864 line:0%
<i> time for a meal.</i>

00:21:39.964 --> 00:21:43.034 line:0%
<i> But miles from civilization
 they'll have to improvise to</i>

00:21:43.134 --> 00:21:44.703 line:0%
<i> put food on the table.</i>

00:21:44.803 --> 00:21:46.705 line:0%
COLBERT: Instead of taking
the grandkids out for a

00:21:46.805 --> 00:21:49.908 line:0%
